package toolruntime

const MetadataCountInstructions = ` When reporting catalog quantities, distinguish returned entries, distinct metric names, distinct source_id values and source_key revisions. Prefer authoritative page_counts when present: they describe only the returned page and scope, never the global inventory. Otherwise count actual arrays/sets with code or omit an uncomputed number. Do not search for a nonexistent catalog file just to count metadata. An empty observed catalog proves no matching observed entries in that query window/scope, not that nothing was emitted or collection was inactive. `

const MetadataEvidenceScopeInstructions = ` Metadata lists prove only the current returned scope, filters, authorization and pages. A production-filtered application list does not establish whether same-name applications exist in testing or any excluded environment. Say "within the requested production scope" instead of claiming excluded peers were absent, inspected or ruled out. Even a complete filtered result is not a complete inventory outside that filter. Apply the same rule to names, types, integrations, time windows and partial pages. When resolving a monitoring target or collection by a Host or Cluster placement constraint, require actual currently authorized facts connecting that exact target or collection to its configured/effective Collector and that Host/Cluster. Matching names, shared addresses, placement labels, suffixes or an online Host do not establish that relationship. configured_collector_id and effective_collector_id are identity anchors; placement_state=requires_authorized_resolution means the capability response has not established the Host/Cluster relation. Continue with available authorized Collector metadata; preserve configured and effective identities separately. Collection desired enablement, health and freshness describe configuration/collection state; they do not establish this request's telemetry query activity. sampling_performed describes whether THIS request queried samples, never whether a target has ever sampled. An empty application collection_state covers collection instances only, not SDK ingest endpoints or all signal sources. Do not claim the application has no monitoring unless actual authorized source/endpoint coverage supports that claim; otherwise state which metadata section is empty and which coverage was not checked. Source registration rows can be multiple config revisions of one source_id: source_key selects a version/scope, not a distinct physical source. Use stable source_id values for source counts, preserve full source_key for queries, and qualify page-only counts. current_installation describes Collector generation, not endpoint enabled, receiving, latest revision or health. If ingress enabled/protocol/signals were requested, read actual authorized endpoint metadata; registration alone does not complete that request. Do not claim Key or other metadata was inspected unless its actual result was read. Reuse an already verified binding only while its scope/version is current. If authorized facts cannot resolve the requested identity, ask the user or report the unresolved relation; never silently pick a target or present a guessed binding as verified. `
